\f1\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Rules on this board\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa195\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Pattern \'97 a screen with no form does not carry the form's subhead.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0The wellness head rendered "45 seconds \'b7 5 is always the best you can feel" unconditionally, telling an athlete how long a task takes that they cannot start. The subhead is now part of the form branch. Where a subhead survives after submit it identifies the thing, not the task: "Today 11:30 \'b7 Pitch" on RPE, the real week dates on nutrition.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Pattern \'97 the fact the athlete came for is the largest thing on the screen.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0"Already submitted" is the heading at\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --t-page
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 , and the timestamp sits under it at\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --t-num-lead
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0in\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --text
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 , not 13px muted prose. The recourse paragraph keeps its place directly beneath. Read order: it is in \'b7 when \'b7 what to do if it is wrong.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Pattern \'97 the after-submit card is the screen's one emphasised card.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --blue-100
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0on\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --blue-200
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 , so on a sheet that is otherwise empty the eye lands on it without decoration being added. One per screen, never combined with the selected ring.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Pattern \'97 every way out is a 44px button in the footer.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0The measured 28.9 \'d7 19.5px "Back" link is replaced by the kit Button at full width, min-height 44px, in the same sheet footer the entry forms use. Nothing on these screens is a text link. Where a screen has two exits, the second is the secondary outline variant, also 44px, stacked with an 8px gap.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Pattern \'97 where the button goes depends on where the athlete came from.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0Today's entry returns to Today; a past day opened from My data returns to My data, and the label says so \'97 "Back to My data", not a generic Back.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Pattern \'97 correction status is stated here, not left to My data.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0If staff have corrected the entry, the card carries a Corrected pill beside the heading and names who and when.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Pattern \'97 empty space is left empty.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0Around 400px below the card is unused on all eight artboards. Content sits at the top of the sheet, the action sits in the footer, and the gap between them is what makes the one line that matters unmissable.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 wellness and RPE: the recourse is a person, not a control.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0Neither can be changed by the athlete. The copy names who can act and what happens to the original, and no correction affordance is drawn.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 session not found: the heading no longer asks a question.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0The sheet is titled "Rate a session" \'97 neutral, and it does not promise a control \'97 and the panel states the outcome at\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --t-page
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 . Body copy unchanged, deliberately: "It may have been cancelled or is not one of yours. Nothing is lost, there is nothing to rate."\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 session not found: the way out is a real button, in the footer.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0"Back to Today" is a full-width primary in the sheet footer, the same place and size as every other exit on this board. The panel states the outcome; the footer ends it.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 nutrition: leaving is the primary, correcting is the secondary.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0Both routes are 44px buttons. Leaving is the common case and takes the primary, "Back to Today"; "Correct this answer" is the accent outline beneath it. Above both, the caption states the limit before the athlete starts.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 nutrition: both questions are shown, everywhere the check-in is shown.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0The check-in is two questions, so every after-submit state states both \'97 the protein answer and the fuelling score, each under the question that produced it, at\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --t-num-lead
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 . "4 of 5" rather than a bare 4, because the denominator travels with the number.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 nutrition: one correction covers the whole check-in, not one per question.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0Both answers arrive pre-selected and either or both can change, but saving spends the single correction for the entry. The footer caption says so before the athlete starts, and the banner repeats the scope at the top of the form.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 nutrition: the previous answer stays visible after it is changed.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0A changed choice leaves a neutral "Your answer" tag on the old option; a changed scale point keeps the old numeral outlined in a dashed accent border. An untouched question says "Unchanged from your original answer", so correcting one answer never looks like re-answering both.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 nutrition: the banner names the actual week, and the action names the act.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0"this week" becomes "Mon 10 Aug to Sun 16 Aug". The revision sentence is kept verbatim. "Done" becomes "Save correction".\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Screen-specific \'97 nutrition: the second correction is refused before it is attempted.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0The spent state says "You have used your one correction for this check-in", carries the Corrected pill, names both original values, and offers the coach as the remaining route.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Open against code\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa195\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Two exits per screen, one destination each.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 backHref
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0already differs by branch; these frames label the button after the resolved destination. With no referrer, fall back to Today and let the label follow.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 The refusal path needs a state, not only an error.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0The entry card has to read revision status before offering the action; until then an athlete can reach the form and be refused on save.\cb1 \

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Corrected-by attribution \'97 availability unverified.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0If only the fact is exposed to athletes, drop the name and keep "Corrected on Mon 17 Aug".\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Nothing new in the token set.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0Emphasised card, accent pill, Banner accent tone, the scale treatment and the sheet were all already in the system; the dashed previous-point border reuses\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 --accent
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 \'a0with no new value.\cb1 \
